[
  {
    "id": "sitl29-tab",
    "type": "tab",
    "label": "SITL 12 Param fan-out set",
    "disabled": false,
    "info": "Build-tier PARAM_SET of ARMING_OPTIONS=1 then sequential fan-out echo-confirm across ArduPilot sysids 1-5 (broadcast refused for PARAM_SET).\n\nARMING_OPTIONS is INT32 on Copter-4.7.0 and the node declares MAV_PARAM_TYPE_REAL32 -- deliberately. ArduPilot ignores the declared type, c-casts the value, and echoes its OWN table type (INT32), so the echo type never equals the sent type. All five members must still report accepted: the wire matcher only compares types on bytewise, where a type mismatch really does mean a garbage store.",
    "env": []
  },
  {
    "id": "sitl29-comment",
    "type": "comment",
    "z": "sitl29-tab",
    "name": "Build PARAM_SET -> sequential fan-out confirm x5 (AP integer param)",
    "info": "Wiring is param [Build] -> fanout [sequential, confirm] per DESIGN.md 10.\nPARAM_SET is sequential-only -- broadcast makes the echoes a storm.\n\nARMING_OPTIONS (INT32) set to 1 while the node declares REAL32. AP stores it correctly and echoes INT32; a sent-vs-echo type equality check would false-unconfirm all five. Bit 0 only suppresses a prearm GCS display, so the fleet is unaffected.\n\nFive ArduCopter on bind 0.0.0.0:14550 -> 127.0.0.1:14551.",
    "x": 300,
    "y": 40,
    "wires": []
  },
